{"id":"122708cc1f5bab8b","group":"73","path":"73/73-thm-ntm-dtm-language-simulation.md","title":"Deterministic and Nondeterministic Recognizability","display":"thm-nondeterministic-turing-equivalence — Deterministic and Nondeterministic Recognizability","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)","book_abbrev":"73","label":"73-thm-ntm-dtm-language-simulation","aliases":["73-thm-ntm-dtm-language-simulation","73-thm-nondeterministic-turing-equivalence"],"display":"thm-nondeterministic-turing-equivalence — Deterministic and Nondeterministic Recognizability","depends_on":["[[73-df-multitape-ntm-semantics]]","[[73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages]]"],"source_id":"HMU2007","source_ref":"§8.4, print pp. 343–352; PDF pp. 365–374; normalized model translation","source_status":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate","reviewed_on":"2026-10-24","legacy_source_id":"HU1979","legacy_source_ref":"§7.5, pp. 159–166; local normalized tape-model interfaces","legacy_source_status":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review","revision_round":"pdf-third-edition-20261024","edition_role":"third-edition-core","third_edition_chapter":8},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Introduction to Automata Theory, Languages, and Computation (Hopcroft, Motwani, Ullman; 3rd ed., 2007)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"73"},{"key":"label","html":"73-thm-ntm-dtm-language-simulation"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>73-thm-ntm-dtm-language-simulation</span><span>73-thm-nondeterministic-turing-equivalence</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-nondeterministic-turing-equivalence — Deterministic and Nondeterministic Recognizability"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"2f2ad13d4f8c1f98\" href=\"?note=2f2ad13d4f8c1f98\" title=\"73-df-multitape-ntm-semantics\">73-df-multitape-ntm-semantics</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"11b19b6d211be8ab\" href=\"?note=11b19b6d211be8ab\" title=\"73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages\">73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_id","html":"HMU2007"},{"key":"source_ref","html":"§8.4, print pp. 343–352; PDF pp. 365–374; normalized model translation"},{"key":"source_status","html":"third-edition-topic-mapped; inherited-local-review; not-a-line-by-line-source-proof-certificate"},{"key":"reviewed_on","html":"2026-10-24"},{"key":"legacy_source_id","html":"HU1979"},{"key":"legacy_source_ref","html":"§7.5, pp. 159–166; local normalized tape-model interfaces"},{"key":"legacy_source_status","html":"local-formalization; source-section-located; proof scope recorded in review"},{"key":"revision_round","html":"pdf-third-edition-20261024"},{"key":"edition_role","html":"third-edition-core"},{"key":"third_edition_chapter","html":"8"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span> 为任意满足 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Alphabet}(\\Sigma)\">\\(\\operatorname{Alphabet}(\\Sigma)\\)</span> 的输入字母表。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{RE}_{\\Sigma}\">\\(\\mathsf{RE}_{\\Sigma}\\)</span> (deterministically recognizable languages, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"11b19b6d211be8ab\" href=\"?note=11b19b6d211be8ab\" title=\"73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages\">73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{NTM}_{\\Sigma}\">\\(\\operatorname{NTM}_{\\Sigma}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L(N)\">\\(L(N)\\)</span> (nondeterministic machines and accepted languages, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"2f2ad13d4f8c1f98\" href=\"?note=2f2ad13d4f8c1f98\" title=\"73-df-multitape-ntm-semantics\">73-df-multitape-ntm-semantics</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}nondeterministic\\text{-}turing\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\left[\nL\\in\\mathsf{RE}_{\\Sigma}\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists N\\in\\{T:\\operatorname{NTM}_{\\Sigma}(T)\\}\\;(L=L(N))\n\\right]\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}nondeterministic\\text{-}turing\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\left[\nL\\in\\mathsf{RE}_{\\Sigma}\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists N\\in\\{T:\\operatorname{NTM}_{\\Sigma}(T)\\}\\;(L=L(N))\n\\right]\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>A deterministic transition is a singleton-valued nondeterministic transition.</li>\n<li>For the converse, a deterministic multitape machine enumerates the finitely branching computation tree breadth first. It accepts exactly when an accepting branch exists; breadth-first dovetailing avoids being trapped on one infinite branch.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"73-df-multitape-ntm-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"2f2ad13d4f8c1f98","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-multitape-ntm-semantics]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages","status":"resolved","id":"11b19b6d211be8ab","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages]]","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages","status":"resolved","id":"11b19b6d211be8ab","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathsf{RE}_{\\Sigma}$ (deterministically recognizable languages, see [[73-df-dtm-recognizable-languages]])","embed":false},{"target":"73-df-multitape-ntm-semantics","status":"resolved","id":"2f2ad13d4f8c1f98","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{NTM}_{\\Sigma}$ and $L(N)$ (nondeterministic machines and accepted languages, see [[73-df-multitape-ntm-semantics]])","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"\\Sigma","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Alphabet}(\\Sigma)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathsf{RE}_{\\Sigma}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{NTM}_{\\Sigma}","display":false},{"tex":"L(N)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}nondeterministic\\text{-}turing\\text{-}equivalence}\\vdash\n\\forall L\\subseteq\\Sigma^*\\;\n\\left[\nL\\in\\mathsf{RE}_{\\Sigma}\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists N\\in\\{T:\\operatorname{NTM}_{\\Sigma}(T)\\}\\;(L=L(N))\n\\right]","display":true}],"bytes":2044,"backlinks":[{"id":"6af52783a9bce985","anchor":"ref-185","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[73-thm-ntm-dtm-language-simulation|Deterministic and Nondeterministic Recognizability]]"},{"id":"ff77be8f80ee06ea","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""}],"outgoing":["2f2ad13d4f8c1f98","11b19b6d211be8ab"]}